  4: /**
  5:  * The golden server notice (ZzzInterface.cpp:491-603). `ReceiveNotice`
  6:  * (WSclient.cpp:1605) routes `ServerMessage` by type: 0 is a notice, 1 goes
  7:  * to the system log, 2 is a guild notice - `GlobalText[483]` wrapped, colour
  8:  * 1 - which also lands in the guild window.
  9:  *
 10:  * The banner is a six-line stack (`MAX_NOTICE`) drawn centred at y = 300 +
 11:  * 13·i in the 640×480 space with `g_hFontBold`. `CreateNotice` pushes at the
 12:  * bottom and scrolls the rest up; a line wider than 256 px is cut in two at
 13:  * the space nearest its middle (`CutText`). `MoveNotices` counts `NoticeTime`
 14:  * down from 300 ticks (12 s at 25 tps) and, at zero, pushes an empty line so
 15:  * old notices drift off the top; every push resets the timer. Colour 0 is
 16:  * (255,200,80) blinking between alpha 128 and 255 every 5 ticks
 17:  * (`NoticeInverse % 10 < 5`), colour 1 is (100,255,200); both sit on
 18:  * black(128).
 19:  */
